    "title": "016: Headless Run (`delphi run`)"
  },
  "summary": {
    "kind": "quote",
    "span": {
      "end": 770,
      "end_line": 18,
      "line": 18,
      "start": 420
    },
    "text": "`delphi run \"<task>\"` runs one task with no terminal and ends with a summary and an exit code, so a script, a CI job or the benchmark runner can use Delphi without a person at the console. It drives the same daemon through the same input grammar as the console (`/build …`, `/council …`, `@role …`, or a plain prompt). It adds no new authority."
  }
